model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "Pool membership and access acknowledgements classify transport failures, non-success responses and receiver timeouts as AccessDependencyUnavailable with HTTP 503 and pool-receiver recovery guidance. SQL, decoding and signing failures remain storage failures. Missing signing configuration refuses recorded pools; operations with no recorded pools need no acknowledgement. App removal preserves typed dependency errors while other hook failures retain AppRemovalUnavailable. Its managed Cloud case proves both tags with transaction rollback and recovery. Hosted and local error messages include the dependency recovery action. The host lifecycle and each affected public API, including native membership and group mutations, preserve the typed failure, transaction refusal, authorization checks and signed-envelope validation. Person revocation covers registered pools available through membership as well as ownership; only owned pools are deleted. Only idempotent pool deletion retries, with the existing two retries and acknowledgement deadline. Durable organization cleanup remains hidden and retains its owner data until the receiver acknowledges, then retries its existing erasure steps. Automatic managed Cloud selection enables the pool-setup fixture for both receiver specifications. Managed Cloud tests scope receiver faults to one pool, prove refused responses and broken connections, preserve access revisions and linked accounts, restore and retry public writes, and verify completed erasure. Architecture build context ee8098a479e261dbc614c34cc037eb9743f20cd1401e08aac7b9a6356d0917ce."
    }
  }
}
